# Frontend runtime (local)

This app's idle local frontend is the **production standalone build** on **:3004**, not `next dev`. Ports **3000** and **8000** are used by other processes — do not bind them. Backend stays on **:8004**. Tmux session: `ananta`, window `frontend`.

Dev and `next build` share `.next`. Always stop the running frontend before switching modes.

## Default (after work, or when not iterating)

```bash
cd frontend
set -a
[ -f .env ] && . ./.env
[ -f .env.local ] && . ./.env.local
set +a
PORT=3004 HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0 npm start
```

`npm start` runs `scripts/start-standalone.sh` (requires a prior `npm run build`). `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is baked in at **build** time; runtime secrets come from `.env.local`. Bake app URL `http://127.0.0.1:3004` and API `http://127.0.0.1:8004/api/v1`.

## While making or evaluating code changes

1. Stop the production server on :3004.
2. `npm run dev -- --hostname 0.0.0.0 --port 3004`
3. When the task is done: stop dev, `npm run build`, start production again on :3004.

Do not leave `next dev` running after the work is finished.
